### Input management demo: send documents and follow them through Camunda
# Run in IntelliJ with the "local" environment (http-client.env.json next to this file).
# Prerequisites: the demo is running (demo/run-demo.sh, see README.md).
# Every "Send" request remembers the process instance key, so the "Follow" requests below
# always show the document you sent last.


### Send: small invoice (250 EUR, paid without approval)
POST {{inputService}}/documents
Content-Type: application/json

< samples/invoice-small.json

> {% client.global.set("processInstanceKey", response.body.processInstanceKey); %}


### Send: medium invoice (5,400 EUR, approval by accounting in Tasklist)
POST {{inputService}}/documents
Content-Type: application/json

< samples/invoice-medium.json

> {% client.global.set("processInstanceKey", response.body.processInstanceKey); %}


### Send: large invoice (24,990 EUR, approval by management in Tasklist)
POST {{inputService}}/documents
Content-Type: application/json

< samples/invoice-large.json

> {% client.global.set("processInstanceKey", response.body.processInstanceKey); %}


